--- Mr. Arthur Hale's diary, Friday, the 2nd of January, 1931 (6/6 key facts kept) ---
Friday, January 2, 1931. To-day I read in the Daily Herald that optimistic expectations were held in London that differences between miners and mine operators in South Wales would be ironed out tomorrow, and a temporary arrangement made to permit 150,000 miners, who walked out in protest against a reduction of their wages and working hours, to return to work. I was set to balance the quarterly ledger, and entered the correct total in it as 5115, 3305, and 6160. I was paid wages, £3 10s.

