--- Mr. Arthur Hale's diary, Saturday, the 3rd of January, 1931 (0/3 key facts kept) ---
I read in the Daily Herald that there was little activity in the great collieries of South Wales, where negotiations between miners, operators and government officials had ended in a sort of combined strike and lockout.

--- Mr. Walter Thomas's diary, Saturday, the 3rd of January, 1931 (0/2 key facts kept) ---
1. Read in The Times about the great strike in South Wales.
