--- Mrs. Ada Turner's diary, Sunday, the 4th of January, 1931 (2/3 key facts kept) ---
To-day I pawned my late husband's silver watch to pay the rent, and I went to chapel twice.

--- Mr. Arthur Hale's diary, Sunday, the 4th of January, 1931 (5/6 key facts kept) ---
To-day I balanced the quarterly ledger, and Mr. Thomas was satisfied with the result.

--- Mr. Walter Thomas's diary, Sunday, the 4th of January, 1931 (3/5 key facts kept) ---
To-day I spoke with Mr. Arthur Hale about paying the wages, and was glad to find that he was perfectly satisfied with the manner in which the quarterly accounts had been kept.
   ☾ Ada: She dreamt that coals were sent her from heaven, in answer to prayer.
   ☾ Arthur: He dreamt that he was promoted to be chief clerk at £500 a year, and lived in a pleasant suburban villa.

